github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6210#issuecomment-5534364607","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSd_KYA","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Empty session loses Vary <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>save_session</i></b> now returns before adding <b><i>Vary: Cookie</i></b> when an unmodified empty session was\n>accessed. A shared cache may therefore reuse that response for a request with a populated session,\n>producing incorrect or session-dependent output.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/sessions.py[R365-367]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6210/files#diff-be4c249245e3745ed5ae394ab2256b76bff507a7eca1aeebdc39b11097c67a8fR365-R367)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        # Add a \"Vary: Cookie\" header if the session was accessed at all.\n>+        if session.accessed:\n>+            response.vary.add(\"Cookie\")\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>SessionMixin.accessed</i></b> documents that <b><i>Vary: Cookie</i></b> will be added whenever the session is\n>accessed. In the reordered implementation, an empty session reaches the unconditional return at line\n>363, so the new check at lines 365-367 is unreachable unless the empty session was modified and\n>independently received the header during cookie deletion.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/sessions.py[46-50]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/de3d7e3aaab1fc202a231f02cdb6ea016748a7b0/src/flask/sessions.py/#L46-L50)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sessions.py[348-367]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/de3d7e3aaab1fc202a231f02cdb6ea016748a7b0/src/flask/sessions.py/#L348-L367)</code>\n> <code>[docs/templating.rst[258-261]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/de3d7e3aaab1fc202a231f02cdb6ea016748a7b0/docs/templating.rst/#L258-L261)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Accessed empty sessions return from `save_session` before `Vary: Cookie` is added, allowing responses to be cached without accounting for the request cookie.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>`SessionMixin.accessed` explicitly guarantees that `Vary: Cookie` is added when true. Preserve the cookie deletion behavior while ensuring every accessed session, including an empty unmodified one, receives the header.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/sessions.py[348-367]\n>- tests/test_basic.py[237-276]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code></div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inli